<title>JAPAN: Japan firms' Oct-Dec capex up 10.0 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan firms' Oct-Dec capex up 10.0 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese companies increased spending on plant and equipment by 10.0 percent in the October-December quarter of 1996 from the same period the previous year, a survey by the Ministry of Finance (MOF) showed on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The quarterly survey covered 839,047 companies, excluding financial institutions and insurance firms, in Japan capitalised at 10 million yen or more.</p>
<p>Year-on-year changes in coporate capital spending, profits and sales were as follows:</p>
<p>				Oct-Dec	July-Sept	Apr-June</p>
<p>Capital spending	  +10.0	   +8.2		+7.3</p>
<p> manufacturing	     +6.7	   +6.3		+4.7</p>
<p> non-manufacturing	+11.5	   +9.2		+8.6</p>
<p>Current profits	   +15.4	  +12.7	     +34.4</p>
<p> manufacturing	    +18.4	  +15.1	     +29.6</p>
<p> non-manufacturing	+12.6	  +10.8	     +37.6</p>
<p>Sales			  +4.9	   +4.4		+5.5</p>
<p> manufacturing	     +6.3	   +7.2		+4.3</p>
<p> non-manufacturing	 +4.3	   +3.4		+6.0</p>
</text>
